# shrink-only — spira-lint/config-env-read-exceptions. One line per file: its repo-relative
# path, then the reason it cannot resolve a registered key through spira_config::process::cfg.
# A line with no reason is refused; a line whose file no longer reads a registered key from
# the environment is refused. Fix the read to remove a line, never add one for new code.
spira-config/src/main.rs the resolver's own CLI: it computes and exports config, so it reads the inputs resolution starts from
spira-config/src/resolve.rs the resolver: env is an input to resolution, not a bypass of it
tsd/src/main.rs tsd sits below spira-config in the dependency graph (cfg() would cycle); callers pass --root resolved
release/src/canary.rs the canary stage is hermetic: it runs against a scratch store and must not see the operator's config
install/src/bin/install.rs the installer is the bootstrap: its environment is the input it renders spira.toml and units from
install/src/bin/units_install.rs bootstrap: runs during install, before the config it would read is rendered
install/src/bootstrap.rs bootstrap: runs during install, before the config it would read is rendered
install/src/orchestrate.rs bootstrap: the install-time render computes the path tail that goes into config
